    englishMeaning: "The branches of this cosmic tree extend downward and upward, nourished by the three modes of material nature (Gunas), with the sense objects as its tender buds. Its secondary roots stretch downward into the human realm, binding the soul through karmic action.\n\nPhilosophical Commentary: The Architecture of the Cosmic Banyan:\n1. Vertical Stratification of Branches: Just as an ancient banyan spreads its limbs across vast spaces, the cosmic tree encompasses all dimensions of existence. The celestial realms are the higher branches sprouted through virtuous Sattvic deeds, while sub-human and subterranean realms represent the lower branches born of Tamasic degradation.\n2. Sense Objects as Seductive Foliage (Viṣaya-pravālāḥ): The five sensory stimuli—sight, sound, taste, touch, and smell—function as the tender green shoots that perpetually entice the embodied soul (Jiva) into sensory indulgence.\n3. The Secondary Roots of Conditioning (Mūlāny anusantatāni): While the primordial Taproot is transcendent Brahman above, the tree drops countless aerial roots downward into human society. These aerial roots are latent psychological tendencies (Vasanas), selfish desires (Kama), and egoic attachments that anchor into worldly action (Karma), binding humanity in the repetitive cycle of transmigration.",
